     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Block mailClient:execution, printServer:lateralMovement and codeRepo:collection. The target is reached through any of four branches: codeRepo, mailArchive, shareMount or dbReplica. Blocking mailClient stops vpnSession and rdpLogin, both AND steps. That in turn stops monitoringHost, hypervisor, secretsManager and serviceAccount, so dbReplica and shareMount become unreachable. Blocking printServer cuts mailArchive. codeRepo must be blocked directly: fileServer stays reachable through browserStore from the entry footholds, and localAdmin stays reachable, so no other single block cuts it. Two blocks cannot work. The codeRepo branch needs its own block (codeRepo or fileServer), and neither of those helps any other branch. The mailArchive branch can only be cut through printServer or its tokenCache/containerHost route, which leaves dbReplica reachable. So the minimum is 3.\"}\n```"
    }
